--   The formal exponential $\mathrm{Exp}_0(a,b) = 2^{a+b}$ of the model
-- statement:
--   For a pair of rationals $x = (a, b) \in \mathbb{Q} \times \mathbb{Q}$, define the real number
--
--   $$\mathrm{Exp}_0(a,b) = 2^{\,a+b},$$
--
--   the real power $2^{r}$ being `Real.rpow` at the real coercion of $a+b$.
--
--   The pair $(a,b)$ is a coordinate vector for the element $a t + b \bar t$ of the rational plane spanned by a transcendental point $t$ on the circle $z\bar z = \rho$ and its conjugate  coordinates are used rather than the elements themselves because $t$ and $\bar t$ are $\mathbb{Q}$-independent, so the coordinate map is a bijection onto the plane, and because the involution then acts simply by swapping $a$ and $b$.
--
--   $\mathrm{Exp}_0$ is the *formal exponential* of the model that shows the analogue of Diaz's conjecture to be false in the purely algebraic setting: it is a homomorphism from the plane into the multiplicative group of the algebraic numbers, it commutes with the involution, its kernel is the divisible line $a + b = 0$, and its image $2^{\mathbb{Q}}$ is torsion-free. Those four facts are stated as separate theorems  this file fixes only the definition.
